# Dependency/build dirs carry NO trailing slash: `foo/` matches only a real
# directory, never a symlink of that name, so a worktree-local
# `node_modules -> <somewhere>` link was swept into a commit by `git add -A`
# (40b6ac6) — the committed link pointed at its own path, and every npm spawn
# under the checkout died with `ELOOP: too many symbolic links encountered`,
# breaking ./scripts/install-local.sh. A slashless pattern ignores both shapes.
node_modules
dist
coverage
# karst config lives at .karst/karst.yml and is committed; only the generated
# worktrees under it are ignored. (Note: worktree.ts excludes the whole .karst/
# in each *service* repo via .git/info/exclude — that asymmetry is intentional:
# service repos never track karst artifacts, but the karst project commits its yml.)
.karst/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json
# Generated Codex lifecycle bridge. Repository-owned files elsewhere under
# `.codex/` remain trackable.
.codex/karst/
# Generated Opencode bridge plugin — written at launch with a per-session hook
# endpoint, so a committed copy carries a dead port + launch id and conflicts
# with every worktree's regenerated one. Rule carries no trailing slash for the
# same reason (see src/runtime/karstExcludes.ts).
.opencode/plugins/karst-*
# Materialized at launch by ClaudeAdapter.materializeApproach — a build product
# of the approach package, never a source.
.karst-plugin/
# The `karst-rpi` workflow skill CodexAdapter materializes from
# renderWorkflowCommand. karst is developed in the repo it also drives, so every
# launch here rewrites it with THIS machine's extension dir, globalStorage
# karst.db and checkout root — and a committed copy is worse than stale: it
# predates GENERATED_STAMP, so writeGeneratedArtifact refuses to clobber it and
# another machine's dead commands survive forever (see agentsTreeGuard.test.ts).
# Named exactly, NOT as `karst-*`: `.agents/skills/karst-graph-engineering/` is
# shipped in the VSIX (BUILT_IN_PACKAGE_PATH) and `.agents/skills/karst-rpi-*/`
# is hand-maintained — both are source.
/.agents/skills/karst-rpi/
*.vsix
.karst-cache
# macOS Finder metadata — binary, per-directory, and rewritten by merely opening
# the folder, so it lands in commits that have nothing to do with it.
.DS_Store
# Per-ticket RPI planning scratch (REQUEST/RESEARCH/PLAN/pm/ux/eng/IMPLEMENT) —
# working notes for a single ticket's implementation, not project documentation.
rpi/
# Supervised-process output. These are written to `.karst/logs/` now
# (src/runtime/serverLog.ts), but karst is developed in the repo it also drives,
# so a run from an older build can still drop one here — and one already reached
# main (`Karst-extention.log`, one line of a service's stdout).
*.log
# Generated by docs/design/stages/harness.mjs — the shipped dashboard webview
# with fake state injected, for measuring the stage track at narrow widths. A
# build product of webview.html, regenerated on demand, never a source.
docs/design/stages/_harness-shipped.html
# The runtime registry. karst is developed in the repo it also drives, so a run
# from this checkout drops its SQLite database (and the transient `-wal`/`-shm`
# sidecars) at the root. It carries whatever tickets and sessions the developer
# had open and its `user_version` trails the branch's SCHEMA_VERSION, so it is
# never a fixture — a named one would live under a test directory.
karst.db
karst.db-shm
karst.db-wal

# Local, uncommitted config (e.g. KARST_REMOTE_HOST for scripts/package-remote.sh)
.env.local
